        "Existing canonical place owner can represent bound camp including party and departure/movement; explicit unbound carrier and distinct ID roles remain policy decisions, not compatibility constraints."
      ],
      "remaining_evidence": [
        "Global exact aliases and distinct frame/trial/challenge owner policy; no absence proof from primary metadata search.",
        "Alternate public/native CaseSiteId admission paths retain their own qualification. The actual canonical factory invalid-component suspicion is excluded only for the assessed bounded producers."
      ],
      "dependencies": [
        "Bound site owner and explicit unbound/bound carrier shape",
        "Native frame Serde adapter and actual binder/reducer guard semantics",
        "Independent journey quantity and any distinct typed ID owner policies"
      ],
      "closure_condition": "Record existing bound-owner repair scope and concrete carrier/ID policy questions, then finish exact aliases and required connected/current contracts. Do not implement.",
      "acceptance_requirements": [
        "Use existing canonical bound camp identity through retained domain state and encode only at native adapter; unbound remains explicit and distinct from zero coordinates.",
        "Distinct referents may reuse a checked component leaf with distinct role owners; sharing a remedy is not an alias.",
        "Actual actor/party/case/contract/destination/revision and retry/optional-mode guards remain intentional."
      ]
    },
